<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Finnish central bank head declines comment on ERM.</title>
<headline>Finnish central bank head declines comment on ERM.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1996-09-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish central bank governor Sirkka Hamalainen refused to comment on Saturday on whether and when the markka may join the European Union's Exchange Rate Mechanism (ERM).</p>
<p>&quot;No comments on ERM,&quot; she told Reuters ahead of a meeting in Dublin of EU finance ministers and central bank heads who are discussing preparations for Economic and Monetary Union (EMU).</p>
<p>Speculation has been intense recently about an imminent Finnish decision to join ERM.</p>
<p>But EU monetary officials have said such a move is highly unlikely this weekend in view of the full agenda of the meeting in Dublin. -- Dublin Newsroom +353 1 4759258</p>
</text>
